{"hw":"ὄντα","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ὄντα</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ὄντα</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">τά</span>, neut. pl. <span class=\"lex-gram\">part.</span> of <span class=\"gk\">εἰμί</span> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">(sum), the things which actually exist, the present,</b> opp. the past and future, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hel.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">14</span> </span>; butalso, </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">reality, truth,</b> opp. that which is not, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Sph.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">263d</span> </span>; <b class=\"lex-tr\">actual objects,</b> <span class=\"gk\">σκιὰς τῶν ὄντων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">R.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">532c</span> </span>, etc.; v. εἰμί. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">that which one has, property, fortune</b> (cf. <span class=\"gk\">οὐσία</span>), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">18.102</span> </span>.</div></div>"}